Subject: Answer a FindService carrying Unicast Flag = 0

vsomeip drops any FindService whose SD Unicast Flag is 0: the else branch
of send_uni_or_multicast_offerservice() is empty, citing SIP_SD_91 ("Find
messages received with Unicast Flag set to 0 (multicast), shall be
ignored"). No solicited OfferService ever leaves the stack for such a Find.

TC8 §5.1.5.4.4 SOMEIPSRV_SD_BEHAVIOR_04 and §5.1.6 SOMEIP_ETS_130 assert
the opposite reading, the one PRS_SOMEIPSD_00268 / 00305 / 00306 / 00307
carries: the server answers a FindService and the Unicast Flag does not
suppress that answer. SD_BEHAVIOR_04 further asserts the answer is
multicast. With upstream behaviour the assertion is unobservable on a
Linux DUT — SD_BEHAVIOR_04 lands `inconclusive_no_offer_after_multicast_find`,
and ETS_130 only ever passes on an unrelated cyclic OfferService drifting
into its listen window.

This patch answers such a Find with a multicast OfferService. The Unicast
Flag = 1 path (SID_SD_826 / SIP_SD_89 / SIP_SD_90) is untouched, so the
half-offer-delay unicast-vs-multicast choice every other case depends on
keeps its upstream behaviour.

The new branch is compile-gated on ENABLE_TC8_ANSWER_MULTICAST_FIND, a CMake
option defaulting to ON. Both readings of the Unicast Flag are deployed: a
consumer whose own specification mandates the SIP_SD_91 drop configures
-DENABLE_TC8_ANSWER_MULTICAST_FIND=OFF through the existing
TC8_EXTRA_VSOMEIP_CMAKE_ARGS seam and compiles the stock branch, instead of
declining this patch or carrying a revert whose text sits on the lines
inserted here. OFF is byte-identical to unpatched vsomeip in this function;
ON is what every harness build and both TC8 cases above see.

The added lines follow the stock SIP_SD_91 comment instead of replacing it, so
the diff is purely additive and every stock line in the branch survives as
context. Measured against a downstream layer that patches this same function:
replacing those two comment lines cost that layer one fuzzed hunk, keeping
them costs it none.

Affects:
  implementation/service_discovery/src/service_discovery_impl.cpp
  CMakeLists.txt
Index: vsomeip/implementation/service_discovery/src/service_discovery_impl.cpp
===================================================================
--- vsomeip.orig/implementation/service_discovery/src/service_discovery_impl.cpp
+++ vsomeip/implementation/service_discovery/src/service_discovery_impl.cpp
@@ -2820,6 +2820,22 @@ void service_discovery_impl::send_uni_or
     } else {
         // SIP_SD_91
         // Find messages received with Unicast Flag set to 0 (multicast), shall be ignored
+#ifdef ENABLE_TC8_ANSWER_MULTICAST_FIND
+        // ... except for TC8 conformance, where SIP_SD_91 above is relaxed:
+        // PRS_SOMEIPSD_00268/00305/00306/00307 require the server to answer a
+        // FindService regardless of the Unicast Flag, and TC8 asserts the multicast
+        // answer. Answer with a multicast OfferService instead of dropping the Find.
+        //
+        // Compile-gated because both readings of the Unicast Flag are deployed: a
+        // consumer whose own specification mandates the SIP_SD_91 drop configures
+        // -DENABLE_TC8_ANSWER_MULTICAST_FIND=OFF and compiles this branch out.
+        // Default ON, so the harness reference DUT is unaffected.
+        //
+        // The stock comment lines above are deliberately kept in place, ahead of
+        // this block: a downstream patch layer whose own hunks carry them as
+        // context then still applies at zero fuzz.
+        send_multicast_offer_service(_info);
+#endif
     }
 }
 
Index: vsomeip/CMakeLists.txt
===================================================================
--- vsomeip.orig/CMakeLists.txt
+++ vsomeip/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -117,6 +117,22 @@ if (ENABLE_SIGNAL_HANDLING)
 set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -DVSOMEIP_ENABLE_SIGNAL_HANDLING")
 endif ()
 
+# TC8 conformance: answer a FindService carrying SD Unicast Flag = 0.
+# ON  => service_discovery_impl::send_uni_or_multicast_offerservice() answers such
+#        a Find with a multicast OfferService, the reading
+#        PRS_SOMEIPSD_00268/00305/00306/00307 carries and TC8
+#        SOMEIPSRV_SD_BEHAVIOR_04 / SOMEIP_ETS_130 assert.
+# OFF => the stock SIP_SD_91 drop, for a consumer whose own specification mandates
+#        ignoring a Find whose Unicast Flag is not 1.
+# Default ON: this is the harness reference DUT's behaviour. The name is the
+# stable contract — it survives renumbering or renaming of the patch that
+# introduces it. Turn it off through TC8_EXTRA_VSOMEIP_CMAKE_ARGS.
+option(ENABLE_TC8_ANSWER_MULTICAST_FIND
+       "Answer a FindService whose SD Unicast Flag is 0 (OFF = stock SIP_SD_91 drop)" ON)
+if (ENABLE_TC8_ANSWER_MULTICAST_FIND)
+set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -DENABLE_TC8_ANSWER_MULTICAST_FIND")
+endif ()
+
 if (NOT MSVC)
     # Sanitizers
     if (ENABLE_SANITIZERS)
